1
00:00:58,057 --> 00:01:00,494
Thanks for looking this
over. You're a lifesaver.

2
00:01:00,577 --> 00:01:03,994
I have to get this press release
revised by the end of the day.

3
00:01:04,077 --> 00:01:06,094
I'm just glad I could help.

4
00:01:06,177 --> 00:01:07,857
Let me know anytime you need a hand.

5
00:01:08,597 --> 00:01:11,914
Even a single word choice could
send our stock prices fluctuating.

6
00:01:11,997 --> 00:01:13,757
Way to ramp up the
pressure all of a sudden.

7
00:01:16,657 --> 00:01:17,661
Hey, um...

8
00:01:17,744 --> 00:01:18,744
Hmm?

9
00:01:21,417 --> 00:01:23,997
I'm really sorry about the other day.

10
00:01:24,710 --> 00:01:25,769
About what?

11
00:01:26,757 --> 00:01:31,557
I know we were drinking, but I
got way too explicit in front of a lady.

12
00:01:32,397 --> 00:01:33,994
Oh, haha.

13
00:01:34,077 --> 00:01:35,634
Don't sweat it.

14
00:01:35,717 --> 00:01:38,577
I haven't had that much
fun drinking in ages.

15
00:01:39,157 --> 00:01:40,157
Oh.

16
00:01:45,355 --> 00:01:46,355
Huh?

17
00:01:47,257 --> 00:01:50,934
Is it possible to see a straight
friend in a romantic way?

18
00:01:51,017 --> 00:01:54,654
I just saw Ueno-san and Kanda-san
coming to work together the other day.

19
00:01:54,737 --> 00:01:56,757
It's not like we're particularly close.

20
00:01:58,577 --> 00:01:59,577
Ah.

21
00:02:00,370 --> 00:02:01,234
Could the person Kanda
was talking about be...

22
00:02:01,317 --> 00:02:03,757
Didn't we agree to stay out of it?

23
00:02:05,717 --> 00:02:09,097
Kanda-san probably hasn't
even figured it out himself yet.

24
00:02:10,697 --> 00:02:12,057
Y-You have a point.

25
00:02:12,557 --> 00:02:15,497
Better safe than sorry, right?

26
00:02:16,697 --> 00:02:17,697
Exactly.

27
00:02:18,397 --> 00:02:19,397
I'm heading out.

28
00:02:28,023 --> 00:02:30,400
Is your friend still staying over?

29
00:02:33,937 --> 00:02:35,817
It's not that I'm avoiding him.

30
00:02:37,017 --> 00:02:38,317
It's just...

31
00:02:55,197 --> 00:02:56,774
I just feel like...

32
00:02:56,857 --> 00:03:00,497
after doing something
like that behind his back,

33
00:03:01,556 --> 00:03:03,850
I can't face Kanda
without feeling terrible.

34
00:03:05,097 --> 00:03:06,577
I have a guilty conscience.

35
00:03:15,517 --> 00:03:16,517
Yeah, still there.

36
00:03:23,117 --> 00:03:25,437
Ueno has his own life,

37
00:03:26,017 --> 00:03:28,637
and he has his own needs, too.

38
00:03:29,877 --> 00:03:31,377
I get all that.

39
00:03:39,457 --> 00:03:40,614
So what on earth

40
00:03:40,697 --> 00:03:42,197
do I even want to do?

41
00:03:44,099 --> 00:03:46,893
(Dad)

42
00:04:53,585 --> 00:04:56,121
"You Should Be The One To Come Kiss Me"

43
00:04:59,117 --> 00:05:00,208
(Episode 4)
Here you go.

44
00:05:09,976 --> 00:05:11,061
Sorry about this.

45
00:05:14,564 --> 00:05:16,094
If everyone has

46
00:05:16,177 --> 00:05:18,277
one or two things

47
00:05:19,237 --> 00:05:21,197
they find hard to talk about,

48
00:05:23,797 --> 00:05:25,534
then for me,

49
00:05:25,617 --> 00:05:27,377
it's my dad.

50
00:05:33,277 --> 00:05:34,294
Kanda,

51
00:05:34,377 --> 00:05:37,194
congrats on winning the gold
prize in the internal competition!

52
00:05:37,277 --> 00:05:38,114
Congrats!

53
00:05:38,197 --> 00:05:39,497
Thanks.

54
00:05:41,617 --> 00:05:42,617
Hey, hey, hey!

55
00:05:42,677 --> 00:05:45,077
Since we're celebrating, let's
get this deluxe sashimi boat.

56
00:05:45,757 --> 00:05:46,757
That's pricey.

57
00:05:47,257 --> 00:05:48,990
Come on, don't be so stingy on payday.

58
00:05:50,317 --> 00:05:54,774
Kanda's proposal was fun
and feasible. It was awesome.

59
00:05:54,857 --> 00:05:56,057
You totally deserved the gold.

60
00:05:56,117 --> 00:05:57,697
It was just a fluke.

61
00:05:58,717 --> 00:05:59,434
Just take the compliment.

62
00:05:59,517 --> 00:06:01,034
I'm telling you, I just got lucky.

63
00:06:01,117 --> 00:06:02,117
No,

64
00:06:02,195 --> 00:06:03,530
I learned a lot from it.

65
00:06:05,717 --> 00:06:06,717
Oh, yeah?

66
00:06:07,830 --> 00:06:10,834
Your sales numbers are way ahead
of everyone else in our year, too.

67
00:06:10,917 --> 00:06:12,038
Wow, that's impressive.

68
00:06:13,417 --> 00:06:16,677
Watching you makes me anxious about
just doing the bare minimum to get by.

69
00:06:18,077 --> 00:06:20,497
Where do you get your drive from?

70
00:06:25,093 --> 00:06:28,897
I'm just a workaholic, that's all.

71
00:06:29,517 --> 00:06:30,877
You're being way too modest.

72
00:06:32,777 --> 00:06:34,414
Anyway, what about that sashimi boat?

73
00:06:34,497 --> 00:06:37,022
Excuse me! Could we get the
deluxe sashimi boat, please?

74
00:06:37,105 --> 00:06:38,982
Certainly. Thank you.

75
00:06:42,617 --> 00:06:44,077
Alright.

76
00:06:44,777 --> 00:06:47,797
Let's keep the party going
at Ueno's place after this.

77
00:06:49,034 --> 00:06:49,554
What?

78
00:06:49,637 --> 00:06:50,714
My place?

79
00:06:50,797 --> 00:06:53,037
You let me crash there last
time when my power went out.

80
00:06:53,457 --> 00:06:54,998
That was only because

81
00:06:55,081 --> 00:06:57,054
you said you had nowhere else to go.

82
00:06:57,137 --> 00:06:58,714
Come on!

83
00:06:58,797 --> 00:06:59,514
Please?

84
00:06:59,597 --> 00:07:00,897
Just for tonight.

85
00:07:03,397 --> 00:07:04,474
Sorry.

86
00:07:04,557 --> 00:07:06,457
Tonight's not a good time.

87
00:07:15,417 --> 00:07:16,994
Looks like you're having a good time,

88
00:07:17,077 --> 00:07:18,077
Eito.

89
00:07:23,109 --> 00:07:24,109
Dad.

90
00:07:31,237 --> 00:07:32,285
How much do you want?

91
00:07:33,677 --> 00:07:35,080
Don't be like that.

92
00:07:35,937 --> 00:07:37,774
I came to see you.

93
00:07:39,084 --> 00:07:41,094
The money is just an afterthought...

94
00:07:41,177 --> 00:07:42,477
I'll go hit the ATM.

95
00:07:47,217 --> 00:07:48,910
Ueno, you go on ahead.

96
00:07:48,993 --> 00:07:49,993
Thanks for tonight.

97
00:07:52,138 --> 00:07:53,138
Excuse me.

98
00:08:18,597 --> 00:08:21,134
I really didn't want Ueno to see that.

99
00:08:21,217 --> 00:08:22,217
Sorry for the wait.

100
00:08:23,837 --> 00:08:25,422
- Sorry...
- It's fine.

101
00:08:35,098 --> 00:08:37,937
Someone asked me to
start a business with them.

102
00:08:39,117 --> 00:08:40,654
Once it gets off the ground,

103
00:08:40,737 --> 00:08:42,316
I'll pay you back with interest.

104
00:08:45,177 --> 00:08:47,485
Still, he probably won't think much of it.

105
00:08:51,557 --> 00:08:54,177
That's just how it is with
other people's family drama.

106
00:08:55,160 --> 00:08:56,344
I'd do the same.

107
00:09:00,957 --> 00:09:03,637
Even if I were a bit surprised,
I'd pretend I didn't see anything,

108
00:09:05,037 --> 00:09:07,557
make small talk at the office,

109
00:09:08,797 --> 00:09:09,883
and just like that,

110
00:09:11,397 --> 00:09:12,397
move on.

111
00:09:20,810 --> 00:09:21,810
Oh.

112
00:09:31,196 --> 00:09:32,489
Found you.

113
00:09:38,153 --> 00:09:39,153
Huh?

114
00:09:39,597 --> 00:09:40,597
What are you doing here?

115
00:09:41,497 --> 00:09:43,197
Are the trains down or something?

116
00:09:44,537 --> 00:09:45,894
No, it's not that.

117
00:09:47,197 --> 00:09:48,717
I was just a little worried about you.

118
00:09:50,777 --> 00:09:52,597
Sorry if I'm overstepping.

119
00:09:56,737 --> 00:09:58,031
I figured tonight,

120
00:09:59,857 --> 00:10:01,437
you'd want someone to drink with,

121
00:10:03,277 --> 00:10:04,577
rather than drinking alone.

122
00:10:12,357 --> 00:10:13,357
Yeah.

123
00:10:15,117 --> 00:10:16,117
Maybe you're right.

124
00:10:28,419 --> 00:10:29,587
(Ueno)

125
00:10:31,965 --> 00:10:34,008
(Can I come over right...)

126
00:10:37,470 --> 00:10:38,470
Oh, right.

127
00:10:39,556 --> 00:10:41,099
It's a bad time for him.

128
00:10:46,646 --> 00:10:47,646
(Sorry, wrong text)

129
00:10:47,677 --> 00:10:48,774
Excuse me.

130
00:10:48,857 --> 00:10:51,757
Your table time is just about up.

131
00:10:52,757 --> 00:10:54,057
Oh, sorry.

132
00:11:53,417 --> 00:11:55,477
Isn't this Ueno's stop?

133
00:12:10,617 --> 00:12:13,399
What am I, some needy attention-seeker?

134
00:12:19,617 --> 00:12:21,115
Even without Ueno,

135
00:12:22,257 --> 00:12:24,160
I can just sleep it off and bounce back.

136
00:12:24,957 --> 00:12:27,897
I can get by just fine.

137
00:12:29,757 --> 00:12:30,808
Even without...

138
00:12:32,437 --> 00:12:33,561
Ueno.

139
00:12:34,754 --> 00:12:35,754
Kanda?

140
00:12:40,377 --> 00:12:41,219
Hey.

141
00:12:41,302 --> 00:12:42,470
What's with

142
00:12:42,553 --> 00:12:43,763
this text?

143
00:12:47,657 --> 00:12:49,160
Yesterday was payday.

144
00:12:50,277 --> 00:12:51,737
Your dad showed up, didn't he?

145
00:12:54,607 --> 00:12:55,650
Are you okay?

146
00:12:58,137 --> 00:12:59,137
Oh.

147
00:12:59,988 --> 00:13:00,988
Uh...

148
00:13:01,948 --> 00:13:02,948
Sorry.

149
00:13:03,908 --> 00:13:06,469
It's nothing, really.

150
00:13:08,037 --> 00:13:09,037
Wait,

151
00:13:09,677 --> 00:13:11,457
how did you know I was here?

152
00:13:15,253 --> 00:13:17,213
Whenever you don't know where to go,

153
00:13:18,217 --> 00:13:19,857
you usually end up wandering around here.

154
00:13:23,417 --> 00:13:24,717
I do?

155
00:13:34,063 --> 00:13:35,314
Oh.

156
00:13:35,397 --> 00:13:38,357
Right, your friend is
still at your place, yeah?

157
00:13:39,402 --> 00:13:42,363
Seeing your face is enough
for me. I'll head home now.

158
00:13:44,057 --> 00:13:45,057
See ya.

159
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:47,243
Kanda.

160
00:13:50,557 --> 00:13:51,581
Are you really

161
00:13:52,665 --> 00:13:53,665
okay?

162
00:13:58,254 --> 00:13:59,254
Man, I'm in trouble.

163
00:14:02,383 --> 00:14:03,676
What is this feeling?

164
00:14:06,721 --> 00:14:08,014
I want to lean on him.

165
00:14:16,877 --> 00:14:18,457
I want him all to myself.

166
00:14:29,117 --> 00:14:30,117
Oh.

167
00:14:30,578 --> 00:14:31,578
Hmm?

168
00:14:32,455 --> 00:14:33,748
I'm out of beer.

169
00:14:34,537 --> 00:14:35,537
You want a drink, right?

170
00:14:36,097 --> 00:14:37,397
Oh, yeah.

171
00:14:38,770 --> 00:14:40,337
Actually, never mind.

172
00:14:42,337 --> 00:14:43,637
No, wait.

173
00:14:44,297 --> 00:14:45,597
I do want one.

174
00:14:49,277 --> 00:14:50,577
Make up your mind.

175
00:14:58,477 --> 00:15:00,191
I'll go buy some.

176
00:15:00,274 --> 00:15:01,334
Oh, I'll come with you.

177
00:15:01,417 --> 00:15:02,502
No need.

178
00:15:03,077 --> 00:15:04,377
Just get some rest.

179
00:15:17,959 --> 00:15:19,293
Ugh...

180
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:24,357
All of a sudden, I don't know
what to talk to him about.

181
00:15:25,133 --> 00:15:27,343
How did I used to act around him?

182
00:15:53,202 --> 00:15:54,929
I knew it'd be here.

183
00:16:20,057 --> 00:16:21,897
I really am just begging for his attention.

184
00:17:15,857 --> 00:17:17,136
Sorry that took so...

185
00:17:33,970 --> 00:17:35,096
Welcome back.

186
00:17:35,997 --> 00:17:37,977
Sorry, did I wake you?

187
00:17:40,797 --> 00:17:42,574
I'm wide awake.

188
00:17:42,657 --> 00:17:44,117
Yeah, right. You were totally out.

189
00:17:47,857 --> 00:17:49,417
You bought a ton of stuff.

190
00:17:51,097 --> 00:17:52,933
The convenience store didn't have
any good snacks to go with drinks,

191
00:17:52,957 --> 00:17:54,616
so I went over to the shopping district.

192
00:17:54,699 --> 00:17:55,614
Seriously?

193
00:17:55,697 --> 00:17:57,157
Thanks for going out of your way.

194
00:17:58,857 --> 00:18:00,497
Oh, let me help.

195
00:18:00,580 --> 00:18:01,789
No, I got it.

196
00:18:02,737 --> 00:18:04,977
I just need to plate them and
pop them in the microwave.

197
00:18:06,017 --> 00:18:07,311
Come on, let me help.

198
00:18:48,297 --> 00:18:49,994
Something really did happen, didn't it?

199
00:18:50,077 --> 00:18:51,134
With your dad.

200
00:18:51,217 --> 00:18:52,217
Huh?

201
00:18:53,057 --> 00:18:54,091
Why do you ask?

202
00:18:54,677 --> 00:18:55,677
No reason.

203
00:18:56,093 --> 00:18:57,386
You just seem a little off.

204
00:18:58,888 --> 00:19:00,973
I'm all ears if you want to talk about it.

205
00:19:03,117 --> 00:19:04,143
No, not at all.

206
00:19:05,353 --> 00:19:07,455
My dad was just his usual self.

207
00:19:16,477 --> 00:19:18,017
Just sit still and behave.

208
00:19:25,665 --> 00:19:26,665
Okay.

209
00:19:37,057 --> 00:19:39,153
These minced meat cutlets are amazing.

210
00:19:40,971 --> 00:19:44,350
I heard the ones from the butcher in
the shopping arcade are really good.

211
00:19:44,850 --> 00:19:45,850
Who told you that?

212
00:19:47,603 --> 00:19:48,896
The internet.

213
00:19:49,855 --> 00:19:50,855
Glad I got them.

214
00:19:53,192 --> 00:19:56,437
I figured you'd like them, Kanda.

215
00:20:07,817 --> 00:20:09,697
Oh, right.

216
00:20:10,334 --> 00:20:11,519
You left this behind.

217
00:20:17,550 --> 00:20:18,776
Here, before I forget.

218
00:20:20,037 --> 00:20:21,037
Oh.

219
00:20:29,812 --> 00:20:32,022
Wanna play video games later?

220
00:20:33,037 --> 00:20:34,757
I haven't bought the game yet, though.

221
00:20:38,821 --> 00:20:40,034
I have it.

222
00:20:40,117 --> 00:20:41,117
Huh?

223
00:20:46,477 --> 00:20:47,777
You bought it?

224
00:20:48,557 --> 00:20:50,416
And it's the exact one I wanted to play.

225
00:20:54,297 --> 00:20:55,754
This guy...

226
00:20:55,837 --> 00:20:58,297
I really can't figure him out sometimes.

227
00:20:58,957 --> 00:21:01,237
He's not quite what you'd expect.

228
00:21:02,537 --> 00:21:04,097
I figured on a day like today,

229
00:21:05,639 --> 00:21:07,239
you'd want someone to have a drink with.

230
00:21:10,297 --> 00:21:11,871
Whether it was back then or today,

231
00:21:12,697 --> 00:21:16,317
how do I put it? There are
surprisingly many sides to him.

232
00:21:20,237 --> 00:21:21,274
What's wrong?

233
00:21:21,357 --> 00:21:22,357
Does your stomach hurt?

234
00:21:28,788 --> 00:21:29,788
Right now...

235
00:21:35,795 --> 00:21:36,795
I really

236
00:21:37,797 --> 00:21:40,417
just want Ueno to spoil me.

237
00:21:46,637 --> 00:21:47,937
By the way,

238
00:21:49,725 --> 00:21:50,868
are you sure this is okay?

239
00:21:51,517 --> 00:21:52,817
What about that friend of yours?

240
00:21:54,717 --> 00:21:55,717
They didn't

241
00:21:56,617 --> 00:21:57,617
come over today.

242
00:22:00,077 --> 00:22:01,077
Oh, I see...

243
00:22:26,011 --> 00:22:27,680
And here I even bought edamame mochi.

244
00:22:28,317 --> 00:22:29,599
What?

245
00:22:29,682 --> 00:22:30,766
The souvenir from Sendai.

246
00:22:31,497 --> 00:22:33,410
It expired, so I just ate it myself.

247
00:22:34,727 --> 00:22:35,855
Oh, right.

248
00:22:42,197 --> 00:22:44,857
Actually, it wasn't a friend.

249
00:22:48,837 --> 00:22:51,397
It was someone I met on a dating app.

250
00:22:54,248 --> 00:22:55,248
How do I put this?

251
00:22:55,877 --> 00:22:59,645
I'd feel weird having a friend
over right after doing that.

252
00:23:06,417 --> 00:23:07,514
Wouldn't it gross you out?

253
00:23:07,597 --> 00:23:09,077
From the guest's perspective, I mean.

254
00:23:10,217 --> 00:23:11,223
Oh...

255
00:23:12,777 --> 00:23:14,137
I wouldn't really know about that.

256
00:23:16,637 --> 00:23:18,777
That caught me off guard.

257
00:23:20,977 --> 00:23:23,417
It's so rare for Ueno to bring
up stuff like this on his own.

258
00:23:24,557 --> 00:23:25,780
Come to think of it,

259
00:23:25,863 --> 00:23:27,156
isn't this the very first time?

260
00:23:28,337 --> 00:23:29,242
Oh.

261
00:23:29,325 --> 00:23:32,786
By the way, this month's new
releases are up on the streaming site.

262
00:23:36,617 --> 00:23:39,217
If they hit it off, will they start dating?

263
00:23:39,777 --> 00:23:43,437
Or are they just friends with benefits?

264
00:23:47,197 --> 00:23:48,517
No, more importantly...

265
00:23:49,417 --> 00:23:51,614
The fact that he doesn't mind me knowing

266
00:23:51,697 --> 00:23:54,757
that he's seeing someone like that means...

267
00:23:57,237 --> 00:23:58,857
To Ueno,

268
00:23:59,757 --> 00:24:01,537
am I just that kind of

269
00:24:03,037 --> 00:24:04,337
good friend now?

270
00:24:08,857 --> 00:24:10,157
This...

271
00:24:11,992 --> 00:24:13,118
It makes me...

272
00:24:15,204 --> 00:24:16,246
It makes me...

273
00:24:18,777 --> 00:24:21,157
At first, I thought there was no way.

274
00:24:21,717 --> 00:24:23,057
But surprisingly, I was into it.

275
00:24:29,718 --> 00:24:29,969
Huh?

276
00:24:30,052 --> 00:24:32,297
Hey, you're spilling it.

277
00:24:34,377 --> 00:24:35,677
Seriously...

278
00:24:40,104 --> 00:24:41,104
Oh.

279
00:24:41,605 --> 00:24:42,605
Hmm?

280
00:24:43,237 --> 00:24:44,537
Hey...

281
00:24:46,317 --> 00:24:47,617
Instead of them...

282
00:24:48,946 --> 00:24:50,030
why can't it be me?

283
